
========================
COMPILATION DEPENDANCIES
========================

* gcc                       (>= 4.9.2)
* g++                       (>= 4.9.2)
* libspnav-dev              (>= 0.2.2-1)
* Irrlicht                  (>= 1.8.1)
* Qt                        (>= 5.3.2)
* ( libqt5x11extras5-dev )
* libusb-1.0-0-dev

    # apt-get install gcc g++ libspnav-dev libirrlicht-dev libqt5x11extras5-dev qtbase5-dev qt5-qmake qttools5-dev-tools qtchooser libqt5x11extras5-dev libusb-1.0-0-dev
    # apt-get install spacenavd spnavcfg

    $ qmake -version
    $ qtchooser -l
    $ qtchooser -qt 5

======================
EXECUTION DEPENDANCIES
======================

* Polhemus Driver
    $ wget ftp://ftp.polhemus.com/pub/Linux_tools/piterm-1.0.4.tar.gz
    $ tar -xzf piterm-1.0.4.tar.gz
    $ cd piterm-1.0.4
    $ ./configure
    $ make
    # make install
    # ls /usr/local/share/PolhemusUsb/
    # cd fw.rules/
    # cp 90-Polhemus_trkr.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
    # udevadm control --reload-rules
    # mount --bind /dev/bus /proc/bus
    # ln -s /sys/kernel/debug/usb/devices /proc/bus/usb/devices
    # reboot

==================
OTHER DEPENDANCIES
==================

* Virtual Box + Handy Linux 
* xrandr + arandx
* xawtv

===============
GUI DEVELOPMENT
===============

* Qt Designer

===========
COMPILATION
===========

$ qmake
$ make

================
EXECUTION LAUNCH
================

1) Terminal 1 : launch application

  ./Assemblies

2) Start Virtual Machine (Handy Linux)

   a) Plug the first SpaceNavigator

   b) Plug the USB wire of the SpaceNavigator in the Virtual Machine

      (3Dconnexion SpaceNavigator [0435])

   c) Launch the client

      sh client_spnav1.sh

* Back to the host, Terminal 2 :

   a) Plug the USB wire of the second SpaceNavigator

   b) Launch the client

      sh client_spnav2.sh




